      "tr_span": "chapters/stat_tests.es.qmd:470-471",
      "proposition": "The English annotates `correlate()` as 'create correlation table (using default pearson)'; the Spanish annotates the same call as 'mantiene las variables numericas de interes' (keeps the numeric variables of interest), which is what the preceding `select()` does, and drops the statement that the default method is Pearson.",
      "reader_consequence": "A Spanish reader is told `correlate()` subsets columns rather than computes the correlation matrix, and never learns that the correlation coefficient produced is Pearson by default, even though the paragraph above offers Pearson, Kendall tau and Spearman rho as choices.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
